nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:1:# NODAL-REALIZATION: kill or attain the six (8,6)/(9,6) types
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:6:## 0. Scope, hashes, and conventions
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:26:- `REPRESENTATIVE` is not `FULL_ACTUAL_EXIT`. A dimension count, a symmetric ansatz, or a one-place (possibly positive-genus) Galindo realization is not a polynomial-nodal witness. If no safe replacement exists the type is typed `OPEN`.
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:31:## 1. Admissibility data common to the six types
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:33:### 1.1 Row `(8,6)`
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:46:Each `#gaps` equals the geometric `δ_aff`. The relation `n_1=4`, `n_2=2`, `4·6=24∈⟨8⟩`, `2c∈⟨8,6⟩`, `c<24` holds on every row. Galindo’s converse realises each `Δ` by *some* degree-8 one-place curve; that curve need not have geometric genus 0, and even a genus-0 realisation need not be nodal.
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:50:### 1.2 Row `(9,6)`
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:61:### 1.3 Parametrization count (both rows)
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:66:## 2. Type (8,6) — (β₁; δ_∞, δ_aff; M_∞) = (21; 10, 11; 22)
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:83:**Plücker.** Projective closure: degree 8, eleven affine nodes, one place at infinity of type `A_{20}` (`μ=20`, `m_p=2`, `r=1`). Class `m=d(d−1)−∑(μ_p+m_p−1)=56−(11·2+(20+2−1))=56−43=13>0`. Hessian degree `3(d−2)=18`, intersection `3d(d−2)=144`. Nodes contribute 8 each classically (`144−88=56` remaining for `A_{20}` plus inflections). No sourced table of the Hessian multiplicity of `A_{20}` was consumed; a negative inflection count is therefore **not** claimed. Orevkov’s bound `d<α m_max` applies to *cuspidal* (all unibranch) rational curves and does not apply to a curve with nodes.
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:91:and the open condition `h_11 ≠ 0`. Each `h_{odd}` is of weighted degree ≤4. Expected: Gröbner basis of a 6-generator complete-intersection-like ideal in 9 variables, degree 4; msolve/Macaulay2 scale (cf. Fujimoto–Suzuki–Yokoyama’s 11-var/17-poly run for `{6,22,17}`). On each maximal component of `V(I_21)` minus `{h_11=0}` and minus the gcd-2 locus (`p,q∈ℂ[t^2]` after a linear change of `t`), compute the 0-cycle of `I_{DP}=(Δp,Δq)` in `ℚ[s,t]/(s−t)` (or in `σ=s+t`, `π=st`): length 11, reduced, with `p'(t)q'(s)−p'(s)q'(t)≠0` at each pair. If some component is nodal, the type is REALIZED (coefficients of one closed point suffice). If every component has a non-reduced or triple fibre, the type is NON-REALIZABLE. Saturation: extract the ideal, assert the ring, and run the positive control `(6,4,3)` from ROW-SWEEP §2 (`I_{DP}` length 3, reduced) and the negative control `(t^8,t^6)` (gcd 2).
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:94:## 3. Type (8,6) — (β₁; δ_∞, δ_aff; M_∞) = (23; 11, 10; 24)
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:105:## 4. Type (8,6) — (β₁; δ_∞, δ_aff; M_∞) = (25; 12, 9; 26)
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:116:## 5. Type (8,6) — (β₁; δ_∞, δ_aff; M_∞) = (29; 14, 7; 30)
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:118:**Admissibility.** `Δ=(8,6,3)`: `2·3=6∈⟨8,6⟩`, `3<24`. `S_aff=⟨3,8⟩`, seven gaps, conductor 14. Germ `(2;29)`, `δ_∞=14`, `M_∞=30`. This is the Galindo-compatible replacement of the charged-review-refuted threat `(8,2,31)` (ROW-SWEEP and M-INF hostile review): `(8,6,1)` fails axiom (2) because `2·1∉⟨8,6⟩`.
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:135:## 6. Type (9,6) — (β₁; δ_∞, δ_aff; M_∞) = (23; 22, 6; 25)
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:167:## 7. Type (9,6) — (β₁; δ_∞, δ_aff; M_∞) = (25; 24, 4; 27)
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:177:**Verdict: OPEN.** Same ring as §6. Ideal `I_(9,6,2)=(k_17,…,k_3)`, open `k_2≠0`, then `I_{DP}` of length 4, reduced, distinct tangents, exclude gcd-3 covers. Two more generators than §6; still degree 3, still msolve-scale. Same controls. The involution count (four `τ`-pairs) is a *candidate* construction, not a witness: emptiness of extra cubic identifications and reducedness of the four pairs are the missing finite checks and can be run as a specialised slice of the same ideal (restrict to `q∈ℂ[t^2+at+b]`, compute the remainder of `p(t)−p(τ(t))` and the resultant that detects extra `q`-fibres).
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:180:## 8. Obstruction toolkit (Plücker, AM, Orevkov, double-point scheme)
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:182:**AM / Galindo.** Every one of the six `Δ` satisfies Theorem 2.1 of Galindo–Monserrat (hashed in §0). Sathaye–Stenerson / Galindo converse realises each by a one-place curve of degree `d`; that is a local-plus-infinity existence theorem, not a genus-0 theorem, and not a nodal theorem (M-INF hostile review §3.2 already recorded this distinction for `(8,6,3)`). Semigroup genera match `δ_aff` and cannot kill a type that is already on the Galindo list. Primitive-generator uniqueness (FSY Lemma 3) distinguishes `δ`-sequences with the same semigroup (`⟨3,8⟩` as `{3,8}` versus `{8,6,3}`): it explains why `(t^3,t^8)` does not attain type `(8,6,3)`, but does not by itself forbid a different parametrization of degrees `(8,6)`.
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:193:Neither mechanism, as a closed-locus phenomenon, kills a type. A type dies only if every component of the characteristic ideal lies on one of these loci or has non-reduced `I_{DP}`.
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:195:**Approximate-root job (FSY Lemma 1).** For a putative polynomial curve with `δ`-sequence `{δ_0,δ_1,δ_2}` the second approximate root `g_2` of the monic-in-`y` equation satisfies `deg_t g_2(x(t),y(t))=δ_2`. Vanishing of all higher `t`-coefficients is a polynomial system in the parametrization coefficients. This is the exact job that FSY ran for `{6,21,4}` and `{6,22,17}` (CAS, hours, weighted LEX). It is the same finite problem as the `h_k`/`k_i` ideals of §§2–7, written in approximate-root rather than leading-form coordinates.
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:198:## 9. Verdict table and residual
nodal-realization-86-96-grok46-20260831.md:215:- Each type has an exact finite CAS spec (ring, ideal, open condition, `I_{DP}` test, positive and negative controls). All six jobs are msolve/Macaulay2 scale, of the same shape as FSY 2006.
