msolve-prep-realization-grok46-20260831.md:564:## 8. Type (9,6)-B — (25; 24, 4; 27), Δ=(9,6,2)
msolve-prep-realization-grok46-20260831.md:566:Charged `I_(9,6,2)=(k_17,…,k_3)`, open `k_2≠0`, `I_DP` length 4. Generators `k_16` through `k_3` plus Rabinowitsch on `k_2=D^2` (so `D≠0`). The involution slice `q∈ℂ[t^2+at+b]` is **not** a separate job: it is a closed subscheme of this ideal (set `Q3=Q1=0` and `P6=P4=P2` as needed) and remains untested at desk, as the charged report states. Cap 14400 s.
