msolve-prep-realization-grok46-20260831.md:968:## 12. Double-point-scheme post-check (`I_DP` reduced-length test)
msolve-prep-realization-grok46-20260831.md:970:For a closed point `(p,q)` in `QQ[t]`, convert divided differences to `(sig,pi)` by the recurrence Delta(t^n) = sig Delta(t^{n-1}) - pi Delta(t^{n-2}). Tests, in order: immersive (`gcd(p',q')=1`); `I_DP` 0-dimensional of degree `N=delta_aff`; radical; tangent form W = p'(t)q'(s)-p'(s)q'(t) nonvanishing on V(I_DP); parameter polynomial F(X)=product (X^2 - sig X + pi) square-free (no reused parameter / triple fibre). No `saturate()`.
msolve-prep-realization-grok46-20260831.md:978:--   N = expected delta_aff.
