    54	```text
    55	p = t^8 + B t^5 + C t^4 + D t^3 + E t^2 + F t + G
    56	q = t^6 + b t^4 + gam t^3 + d t^2 + e t + f
    57	```
    58	
    59	Ring `R0=ℚ[B,C,D,E,F,G,b,gam,d,e,f]` (11 vars). Weights: `B↦3,C↦4,D↦5,E↦6,F↦7,G↦8,b↦2,gam↦3,d↦4,e↦5,f↦6`, so `p` (resp. `q`) is weighted-homogeneous of degree 8 (resp. 6). Optional gauges `f=0` and `gam=1` (on `gam≠0`) are **not** imposed; they are a case-split, not the charged ring.
    60	
    61	Binomial split, `p_low=p−t^8` (deg ≤5), `q_low=q−t^6` (deg ≤4):
    62	
    63	```text
    64	p^3 = t^{24} + 3 t^{16} p_low + 3 t^8 p_low^2 + p_low^3
    65	q^4 = t^{24} + 4 t^{18} q_low + 6 t^{12} q_low^2 + 4 t^6 q_low^3 + q_low^4
    66	H = p^3 − q^4
    67	```
