   170	
   171	**Even-odd closed locus (desk).** Same odd/even ansatz with `c=0`. For remainder degree 2 one needs `h_4=0` and `h_2≠0`, hence `C=0` and `D≠0`. Substituting `A=3a/2` and the `h_{14}` formula for `B` into `h_{12}=h_{10}=h_8=h_6=0` yields, on `a≠0`, an inconsistent pair `h_8=a^5/96≠0` after the unique solution of the earlier equations; on `a=0` one gets `b=0`, `D=0`, the cover `(t^9,t^6)`. Thus there is **no** even-odd polynomial curve of this type. Again this kills a construction, not the type.
   172	
   173	**Square-root / involution construction.** If `2∈S_aff` then some `r∈ℂ[p,q]` has degree 2. Completing the square, `r=t^2` and `q` is a polynomial in `r` of degree 6, hence even, returning to the killed locus unless `p` supplies mixed terms *and* `r` is not exactly `t^2` in the Tschirnhausen chart of `p`. The involution `τ(t)=−t−a` of a genuine quadratic `r` forces `q(t)=q(τ(t))` identically when `q∈ℂ[r]`; the equation `p(t)=p(τ(t))` is degree 9 and `τ`-invariant, hence contributes `(9−1)/2=4` unordered pairs plus the fixed point of `τ`. That is exactly `δ_aff=4` *if* those four pairs are ordinary nodes and the cubic `r↦q(r)` contributes no extra identifications with matching `p`. Extra identifications are the generic behaviour of a cubic (3-to-1). Forcing them empty is a closed condition on `p` of expected codimension equal to the number of extra pairs, not evaluated at desk. If that condition holds, this *would* be a nodal realisation; it is not exhibited.
