    20	each positive generic meridian to a transposition.  Then no such `B` exists.
    21	
    22	The complete prime iterated-knot census at genus four has seven topological
    23	rows:
    24	
    25	```text
    26	T(2,+/-9),
    27	T(3,+/-5),
    28	C_(2,+/-5)(trefoil or mirror),
    29	C_(3,+/-2)(trefoil or mirror),
    30	C_(4,+/-1)(trefoil or mirror),
    31	C_(2,+/-1)(T(2,5) or mirror),
    32	C_(2,+/-1)(C_(2,1)(trefoil) or mirrors).              (0.1)
    33	```
    34	
    35	The one-place semigroup condition leaves exactly four conductor-eight
    36	delta-sequences:
    37	
    38	```text
    39	(9,2),       (5,3),       (6,4,5),       (9,6,2).     (0.2)
    40	```
    41	
    42	They correspond respectively to the first four rows of (0.1).  Exact
    43	standard-braid enumeration removes the first three: their numbers of
    44	labelled full-`S4` meridian-transposition colorings are `0,0,0`.  Every
    45	sign/chirality version of the last row has `144` such colorings, so boundary
    46	colorability alone does not remove it.
    47	
    48	The new load-bearing calculation removes that last row by the normalization
    49	fibres, not by a determinant or boundary coloring.  Every polynomial
    50	parametrization in the `(9,6,2)` row is equivalent, under affine changes of
    51	the parameter and target coordinates, to
    52	
    53	```text
    54	U=t^6+8*t^2,
    55	V=t^9+12*t^5+24*t,                                    (0.3)
    56	V^2-U^3-64*U=64*t^2.                                  (0.4)
    57	```
    58	
    59	Since
