xmodel/m-inf-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.log:6438:+Thus the corresponding local `8`-minimal sequence is `(8,2,29)`.  Conversely `(8,2,31)` would force affine delta-sequence `(8,6,1)`, which fails axiom (2) because `2*1` is not in `<8,6>`.  It is not merely “unrealized” at type `(8,6)`; it is incompatible with the cited theorem.  The genuine numerically admissible but rationally unrealized threat is beta 29 (and also 25, 23, 21), not 31.  Galindo's converse does automatically realize `(8,6,3)` by a degree-8 one-place curve; what is not automatic is normalization `A^1` with seven affine delta units.  The charged explanation based on possible incompatibility of degree-3 cancellation with degrees `(8,6)` is therefore also wrong.
