xmodel/m-inf-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.log:11267:+At `d=8`, one individual noncoprime row does close after Piece 1.  For `(8,2)`, `a=6`, `beta_1=8`, and the conductor is `beta_2+27`; `delta_aff>=1` gives `beta_2<=13<16`, hence `M_infty<=18<=21`.  But `(8,4)` and `(8,6)` retain admissible numerical threats: delta-sequences `(8,4,6,3)` and `(8,6,3)` convert to transverse last numerators 19 and 29, against targets 18 and 20.  Thus no blanket `d>=8` closure fires.  “Does not fire” must not be read as “no individual degree-8 row can be proved.”
